# Which registered agents get an executor process. Copy to fleet.yaml and edit.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING AN AGENT.
#
# 1. This file declares intent; `agent_runtimes` records fact. Generating
#    containers from the table instead would be circular: the row records where
#    a process is, so a process started from the row cannot be what created it,
#    and a stale row would perpetuate itself. `agent-control-fleet doctor`
#    is the reconciliation between the two, and it fixes nothing.
#
# 2. One agent is one process. The SDK holds a single agent per process and the
#    ADK plugin refuses to initialize under a second name, so eight agents here
#    means eight containers. Nothing publishes a host port: the executor's HTTP
#    API has no authentication of its own, and the only real control is that its
#    port is reachable from the server's network and nowhere else.
#
# 3. `agent_name` is also a directory name inside the container. ADK routes on
#    the folder, not on App(name=...), so the name must be lowercase letters,
#    digits and underscores. A hyphen or a colon is accepted by the server and
#    unroutable as an app, which surfaces as a 500 on the first turn rather than
#    as anything an operator can read.
#
# 4. `web_tools` is the Exa toolset, on by default. An agent with an outbound
#    fetch tool is an SSRF pivot onto the network its own executor sits on, and
#    with company knowledge also on it is a retrieval-plus-egress pair. Turning
#    both on is a decision; see docs/plans/agent-fleet-topology.md section 3.2.
#
# The model base URL is NOT configured here. It is computed from the live
# network gateway at `up` time, because the gateway is what the host is from
# inside these VMs and host.docker.internal resolves to nothing on this runtime.
# AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_MODEL_BASE_URL overrides it and refuses a loopback address.
#
# Resources are environment too. Each executor is a VM, and the runtime default
# is 1024MB and 4 CPUs apiece, which at eight agents reserves 8GB and 32 CPUs to
# run a process measured at 37MB idle and 105MB through a turn with a tool call.
# The fleet asks for 512MB and 2 CPUs instead; AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_MEMORY
# and AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_CPUS override that.
#
# Credentials are environment, not file: AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_REGISTER_API_KEY is
# the admin key the two one-shot jobs hold, and AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_API_KEY
# is the key every executor runs on. `up` refuses to start anything when the
# second cannot claim a halt, because an executor that cannot has lost the
# operator STOP button while the console still shows the halt recorded.

version: 1
image: agent-control-executor:local

defaults:
  web_tools: true

# Adding an agent is a reviewed decision about a container that runs
# model-driven code. Keep this list to agents somebody is actually using.
agents:
  - agent_name: marketing_researcher
  - agent_name: marketing_copywriter
  - agent_name: sales_outreach_drafter
    web_tools: false
